+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Authenticated customers currently lose carts across sessions, cannot reliably calculate totals, receive unusable server errors from checkout validation, and see incorrect order-list pagination metadata. These defects undermine the logged-in shopping flow and can cause customers to abandon purchases.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Associate carts created or modified through authenticated cart requests with the authenticated customer.
+- Make the authenticated current-cart endpoint select only that customer's latest uncompleted cart and return 404 when none exists.
+- Calculate authenticated cart totals using the customer's delivery address and enforce cart ownership with 404 for other customers' carts.
+- Return HTTP 400 with the expected order amount for authenticated checkout payment mismatches, without creating an order; allow matching payments to complete and retire the current cart.
+- Correct authenticated order-list ownership, newest-first ordering, `recordsTotal`, and page-count metadata based on the requested `count`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `authenticated-customer-shopping`: Persistent, customer-scoped cart, total, checkout, and order-list behavior for logged-in customers.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected Spring MVC APIs under `sm-shop`, cart and order facades/services in `sm-shop` and `sm-core`, cart/customer ownership and order pagination queries, HTTP error handling, and integration tests for authenticated customer flows. Guest endpoints retain their existing behavior.
